**Summary:** The change updates the cache layer so that every key is computed with the sorted
inputs, and the test suite now covers the path. **Details:** The handler (in the server package)
reads all of the inputs, sorts them, and hashes the result: this ensures that one key is produced for
each distinct set of inputs, with the ordering no longer affecting the outcome.
-- hit/review-reply whole --
## Changes

The existing behavior is preserved for all of the other callers (the CLI, the daemon and the
console), and the documentation reflects the new contract as well: every caller receives the same
result regardless of the order in which the inputs arrive, which ensures that the cache remains
consistent across all of the supported platforms and configurations.
